  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "\\text{polya\\_cyclic\\_fixed\\_count}: |\\{\\text{colorings } f : \\mathbb{Z}/d\\mathbb{Z} \\to \\text{Fin}\\,k \\mid \\sigma \\cdot f = f\\}| = k^{\\gcd(\\text{ord}(\\sigma), d)}",
    "plain": "In the Burnside/Pólya counting framework, a coloring of $d$ positions with $k$ colors is \"fixed\" by a cyclic permutation $\\sigma$ if $\\sigma$ maps each coloring to itself. The number of such fixed colorings equals $k^{\\gcd(\\text{ord}(\\sigma), d)}$.",
